* Averaged (state-space / PWM-switch) DC-DC converter cores, continuous conduction mode (CCM) only. Project-authored.
* The switch and diode are replaced by their period averages (Vorperian PWM switch, Erickson & Maksimovic ch. 7):
*   buck:  v(sw) = d * v(vin)      current drawn from vin = d * iL
*   boost: v(sw) = (1-d) * v(out)  current delivered to out = (1-d) * iL      (d = D + v(ctl), duty ratio)
* iL flows through the inductor L and its series resistance RL (inductor DCR plus switch/diode conduction resistance,
* lumped). There is no switching ripple, no switching or diode or core loss, and no discontinuous mode: the averaged
* inductor current may go negative at light load (it behaves like a synchronous converter), and nothing limits d.
* rt2 is rt through a 0 V source: the B sources drive rt2 so that reading V(.,rt) is not an algebraic loop on their own node.
* Pins: vin, rt (return), out, ctl. ctl adds directly to the duty ratio (1 V = 100 % duty) for modulation or a feedback loop.
.subckt bench_buck_avg vin rt out ctl params: D=0.5 L=100u RL=20m
Rctl ctl rt 1g
Vr rt2 rt 0
Bsw swp rt2 V=(D+V(ctl,rt))*V(vin,rt)
Vs swp swl 0
L1 swl x {L}
Rl1 x out {RL}
Bin vin rt2 I=(D+V(ctl,rt))*I(Vs)
.ends bench_buck_avg
.subckt bench_boost_avg vin rt out ctl params: D=0.5 L=100u RL=20m
Rctl ctl rt 1g
Vr rt2 rt 0
L1 vin x {L}
Rl1 x y {RL}
Vs y sw 0
Bsw sw rt2 V=(1-D-V(ctl,rt))*V(out,rt)
Bout sw out I=(1-D-V(ctl,rt))*I(Vs)
.ends bench_boost_avg
* fixed-duty wrappers: ctl on an internal node held at rt by a 0 V source
.subckt bench_buck_fixed vin rt out params: D=0.5 L=100u RL=20m
Vz z rt 0
X1 vin rt out z bench_buck_avg D={D} L={L} RL={RL}
.ends bench_buck_fixed
.subckt bench_boost_fixed vin rt out params: D=0.5 L=100u RL=20m
Vz z rt 0
X1 vin rt out z bench_boost_avg D={D} L={L} RL={RL}
.ends bench_boost_fixed
